{
  "name": "ec-gpu",
  "description": "ec-gpu is a Rust-based framework for generating and executing CUDA and OpenCL kernels optimized for finite-field and elliptic curve arithmetic. It provides a compile-time code generation pipeline that produces optimized fatbins or source strings for cryptographic primitives such as Fast Fourier Transforms (FFT) and Multi-Scalar Multiplication (MSM). The system is designed to accelerate zero-knowledge proof systems by offloading heavy algebraic computations to heterogeneous hardware with minimal runtime overhead.",
